 "result_text": "I added a \"Delete All\" button to the contents view. It deletes every item in the folder in one click, after a confirmation prompt. I only checked that the module imports. I haven't run the button in a ZMI or run any tests.\n\n- **Button:** in `contents.dtml`, next to \"Delete\". It only shows for users with the \"Delete objects\" permission, the same as \"Delete\".\n- **New method:** `manage_delAllObjects` in `BTreeFolder2.py`. It calls `manage_delObjects` with every id in the folder, so the usual deletion checks and events still run. It redisplays the contents view with an \"All items deleted.\" message.\n\nFor a folder with very many items this runs as one transaction, so it could be slow or memory-heavy. I didn't test it on a large folder.\n\nI didn't change any tests.",
